{"title":"2021 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1 Part C","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1\" title=\"2021 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_C&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine the positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/f/77f8ca43073c401b0160fc5f1d6b1a2987d9e244.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(20 - n)(20 + n) = 391$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"184\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_C&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bb21f5d3ce6c374e7f3dadfa12bcc7092e9f6f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a - b)(a + b) = a^{2} - b^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"188\" height=\"21\" />, so:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/d/a8dd6ef340a9dcbf37b7e1ef74545b0a1db42431.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$400 - n^{2} = 391$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/c/e5cc3f88ed1d219509381fd6285b775cf175e5bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^{2} = 400 - 391 = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"155\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/9/139fc55aa106c924b61588a90aa0e9e082354186.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\pm \\sqrt{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"21\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/9/a193a8aedbe40e20419055ad70bbd2c07ca47d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pm 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is positive, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/d/a8d9374761dfa796fbdb84fe5ef269020a9e8d9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{n = 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"57\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1_Part_C&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/b/80b138c9bb0eda1298fb8ba7c41f2af944fc38db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 - n$\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/f/4afc6b487e57e74000c11465094eda319d6273c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> must both be integers, meaning that we can look at the factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/2/1526a8aa34532603d1dff95e72fa7138c6c0fb06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$391$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> and see where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/b/80b138c9bb0eda1298fb8ba7c41f2af944fc38db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 - n$\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/f/4afc6b487e57e74000c11465094eda319d6273c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> would be equal to those factors. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is positive meaning that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/f/4afc6b487e57e74000c11465094eda319d6273c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> is positive, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/b/80b138c9bb0eda1298fb8ba7c41f2af944fc38db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 - n$\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" /> is also positive. This means that we're specifically looking at positive factors.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/2/1526a8aa34532603d1dff95e72fa7138c6c0fb06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$391$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/e/b5eba286623f3f19e633149f53a0f05fd2a1495a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17 \\times 23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />, so this means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/a/afad956540f9e4a1e0c0557648c994facffac3f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 - n = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"86\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a89e6d2737f7958003f98ec65aac457d4f2922.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 - n = 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"96\" height=\"15\" /> (since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/b/80b138c9bb0eda1298fb8ba7c41f2af944fc38db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 - n$\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" /> would be smaller than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/f/4afc6b487e57e74000c11465094eda319d6273c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" />). This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c342b01f0cdef0f23d11a2bc9c5aa67f6d83ccb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/e/8aeed81ffe5071b2d5d291bca220b3480da708cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />. However, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/e/8aeed81ffe5071b2d5d291bca220b3480da708cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/c/19cae06111869e06a29e25f4c0fe0112f6d8f8f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 + n = 39$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"96\" height=\"15\" />. This means that the product would not be equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/2/1526a8aa34532603d1dff95e72fa7138c6c0fb06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$391$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/d/a8d9374761dfa796fbdb84fe5ef269020a9e8d9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{n = 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"57\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018063601\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.016 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.028 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 121/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 78/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5223/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.937      1 2021_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1\n100.00%    5.937      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37414:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018063601 and revision id 289136. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}